.TH RECONFORGE 1 "August 2026" "ReconForge v0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reconforge \- Offline reconnaissance analyzer and planning tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reconforge
[\fITARGET\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B reconforge
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ReconForge is an offline log analyzer designed for authorized penetration testing environments. It imports raw outputs from Nmap, Gobuster, and other security tools, normalizing and correlating them. Additionally, it offers an interactive planning mode capable of generating structured execution plans based on provided IPs and URLs without executing external network calls directly.
.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
Running \fBreconforge\fR without arguments launches the interactive mode, prompting for:
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBMode\fR: Standard Recon or WAF-Aware Low-Impact Recon
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBTarget Type\fR: IP Address or URL
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBPort Configuration\fR: Default or Custom
.SH IP MODE
You can quickly generate an execution plan for an IP by passing it directly:
.br
.B reconforge 10.48.159.132
.SH URL MODE
Pass a URL using the \fB-u\fR or \fB--url\fR flag:
.br
.B reconforge -u http://10.48.159.132:5000
.br
ReconForge will parse the scheme, IP, host, and port automatically.
.SH TARGET NORMALIZATION
ReconForge parses and normalizes targets. For example, \fBhttp://10.0.0.1:5000\fR will correctly populate the IP field (10.0.0.1) and Port field (5000) inside the underlying model, ensuring service-aware tool execution planning.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B Standard Recon
Plans default enumeration using all applicable installed tools.
.TP
.B WAF-Aware Low-Impact Recon
Configures the execution plan constraints to respect rate-limits, Retry-After headers, and avoid duplicate/evasive requests.
.SH TOOL REGISTRY
ReconForge maintains an internal registry of supported tools and their adapters.
.br
Check availability with:
.br
.B reconforge tools
.SH OFFLINE ANALYSIS & SESSIONS
.B reconforge import <dir>
Imports scan results and stores them in a session.
.br
.B reconforge sessions
Lists historical sessions.
.SH REPORTS
.B reconforge show current
.br
.B reconforge report current --format html
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
reconforge
reconforge 10.48.159.132
reconforge -u http://10.48.159.132:5000
reconforge -u https://example.com
reconforge 10.48.159.132 --mode low-impact
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error.
